+// OWNRT_TP_XTAIL (lab 2026-10-31, research/tp/xtail-2026-10-31; default off): the direct exchange of a row-split dense
+// GEMV (OWNRT_TP_HC_SPLIT) in the GEMV's own launch instead of a separate tp_xgather kernel.
+//
+// Rows: every subgroup runs dense_v2::bf16_rows<R,U> unchanged (same matrix selection by static indices as
+// bf16_multi_static), so every output value is the one the separate-exchange path computes. The split matrix writes
+// its rows straight into the card's offset of the whole output y (the tp_xgather's local destination); afterwards the
+// work-item that stored a row copies the stored 32-bit word to the same row of the peer card's y (the tp_xgather's peer
+// destination). Other matrices of the launch (the HC low's 4-row inject) store locally only, as before. The peer
+// stores are spread over the groups (token hc) or made by the counting-complete group (token hcl), see body().
+//
+// Exchange protocol: single_device.cpp submit_exchange, mode 0, unchanged except that the work-groups are the GEMV's:
+// - every work-item, after its stores: atomic_fence(release, system); then a work-group barrier;
+// - work-item 0 of each group: fetch_add(1, acq_rel) on this site's local counter (device scope); epoch = old/groups+1;
+//   the group whose increment completes the epoch (last) does fence(acq_rel, system), stores the epoch into the peer's
+//   flag word for this site, fence(release, system), then (unless this card's abort word is set) polls its own flag
+//   word with system-scope atomic loads, at most `cap` polls; a timeout sets the sticky error, the abort word and the
+//   timeout counter, otherwise fence(acquire, system). The wait counters (waits, spun, spin_sum, max_spin) as there.
+// The consumer of y is the next launch on the card (a fresh kernel), as after a tp_xgather. Stores always happen.
+// The last group waits only after every group of the launch has stored, fenced and counted, so no group of this
+// kernel can be waiting to be scheduled behind it.
